  "result": "Perfect! I've found the document that records the decision. **ADR-018** is the architectural decision record that documents:\n\n1. **The decision**: Queue webhook deliveries with capped exponential backoff instead of inline delivery\n2. **The alternatives weighed**: \n   - Inline delivery inside the webhook handler (the original ADR-005 sketch)\n   - Fixed-delay retry instead of exponential backoff\n   - Unlimited retry attempts\n3. **The reasoning**: The Context section explains that inline delivery would cause slow or unreachable webhook endpoints to stall the original request (like issue status changes), violating REQ-154. The team also needed proper retry semantics with exponential backoff and attempt ceilings.\n\nThe document also references ADR-005 (which sketched the original inline approach) and how ADR-018 supersedes that design.\n\nANSWER: docs/adr/ADR-018-webhook-retry-policy.md",
